/-!
# Collection, full block kernels, and the genuine radical quotient

This interface supplies the reverse radical collection theorem, its source
setwise-product description, stability of every octad block, and the full
kernel product before and after applying the literal quotient by `K`.
The resulting relative-kernel quotient acts faithfully on the actual block.
The action statements assume only the three signed-vector laws of 29.12.

The order `2^13`, extraspeciality, and the remaining normality and `EPlus`
structure calculations are not yet asserted here. Irreducibility and fixed
spaces belong to the separate weight-space development.

Source: Aschbacher, *Sporadic Groups*, 14.4–14.5, Section 27, and 29.13(4),
printed pp. 61–62, 144, and 160–161.
-/
